Chez Scheme: release the frames that an escape passes (c/schlib.c, S_call_help)

When Scheme unwinds past C frames (an error raised through a foreign call: a C++ binding that
raises, or a callable that raises), S_call_help is reached again by longjmp ("case 1"), and its loop
is meant to unlock the code objects of those frames and free their jump buffers. The line
`CCHAIN(tc) = yp;` before the loop sets the chain to the frame being returned to, so the loop
walks only that one frame: the jump buffers (about 200 bytes) and the locks of every frame that was
escaped past are never released. Removing the line lets the loop start at the current chain, as its
comment says.

Found with valgrind (200 bytes lost per error in S_call_help) in CREST, 2026-11-12. The same line is
in upstream cisco/ChezScheme main (d533f2e). Not applied on Windows: the comment in S_return says
that platform may need the full chain for unwind handling, and it is not tested there.

diff --git a/c/schlib.c b/c/schlib.c
index 2be486d0..5d519b54 100644
--- a/c/schlib.c
+++ b/c/schlib.c
@@ -276,7 +276,6 @@ void S_call_help(ptr tc_in, IBOOL singlep, IBOOL lock_ts) {
             break;
         case 1: { /* normal return */
             ptr yp = FRAME(tc, 1);
-            CCHAIN(tc) = yp;
             {
               /* unlock code objects that we're escaping past */
               ptr xp;
